UI/UX Audit Report — Employee Portal
1. EmployeeLayoutClient.tsx
Layout & Structure

Uses fixed inset-0 with overflow-hidden for the shell — correct PWA pattern, prevents body scroll bleed.
pb-24 on <main> accounts for the mobile bottom nav bar — good.
The AppHeader visibility logic is broken: the outer div has hidden md:block, but then a conditional block class is added for specific routes. Because Tailwind applies classes in order, hidden md:block wins on mobile regardless of the inner conditional — the header will never show on mobile even for the listed routes. This is a real rendering bug.
Loading State

Loading spinner uses a custom "P" logo + Loader2 + text — clean and on-brand.
No aria-live region or role="status" on the loading screen — screen readers won't announce it.
Auth / Session Logic

Session is read from sessionStorage first, then localStorage as fallback — reasonable offline strategy.
On server errors (500+), the session is silently retained with only a console.warn. No user-facing feedback that auth verification failed.
No timeout on the fetch('/api/auth/me') call — a hanging network request will leave the user on the loading screen indefinitely.
Accessibility

No <SkipToContent> link.
No role="main" on the <main> element (though the tag itself is semantic).
2. AppSidebar.tsx
Desktop Sidebar

Collapse/expand is smooth with CSS transition-[width] — good.
Collapsed state shows only icons with title tooltip — acceptable but no aria-label on nav links in collapsed mode (only title, which is not reliably announced by screen readers).
Section headers (text-[9px]) are extremely small — 9px is below the WCAG minimum readable size and will fail contrast checks on most monitors.
Active state uses bg-primary-500 with white text — likely passes contrast, but not verified against the actual primary-500 value.
The Approvals badge count is only shown for role === 'admin', which is correct.
Mobile Bottom Nav

hideMobileNav logic: the sidebar bottom nav is hidden on dashboard/attendance/daily-report/profile/settings when forceVisibleOnMobile is false. But EmployeeLayoutClient always passes forceVisibleOnMobile={true}, making the hideMobileNav logic permanently bypassed for the employee portal. This means the sidebar nav and the page's own bottom tab bar will both render simultaneously on those pages — a double navigation bar bug.
Bottom nav items have min-w-[56px] — adequate touch target width, but height is only h-16 (64px) for the bar, and individual items have py-1 padding. The actual tap target for each icon+label is approximately 44–48px tall, which is borderline for WCAG 2.5.5 (44×44px minimum).
The "More" button label is "More" — generic, not descriptive for screen readers. Should be "More navigation options" (the aria-label is set, which is good).
text-primary-505 appears in the active link class — this is a typo/non-existent Tailwind color token. It will silently fall back to no color, meaning the active state color may not apply correctly.
More Drawer (Bottom Sheet)

Drag handle is purely decorative (div) with no swipe gesture handler — the handle implies swipe-to-dismiss but only click-on-backdrop dismisses it.
max-h-[60vh] on the overflow items container is good to prevent overflow on small screens.
Grid of 3 columns for overflow items — labels are text-[10px] with truncate, so long labels will be cut off silently.
No role="dialog" or aria-modal="true" on the bottom sheet — screen readers won't treat it as a modal.
Focus is not trapped inside the drawer when open.
Logout

Uses ConfirmationModal — good pattern, prevents accidental logout.
Clears all known session keys from both sessionStorage and localStorage — thorough.
